course: dictionary
lesson: 7092
title: Vocabulary in context: peace
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Peace is a noun with three main meanings: a time with no war or fighting, a calm and quiet feeling, and getting along with others without arguing. To choose the right meaning, read the words around it. «After the Battle of Kadesh, Egypt and the Hittites signed one of the oldest known peace treaties» tells you the countries stopped fighting, so peace means a time with no war.
explain: Peace can also mean calm and quiet, like a room where nobody is shouting. If a sentence is about a quarrel, peace probably means getting along again, as in making peace after an argument.
explain: Check your meaning by swapping it into the sentence. If "a time with no war" still makes sense in place of peace, you have chosen well. Peace is uncountable, so we say some peace, not two peaces.
fact: Peace is a noun, and it is uncountable: we say some peace, not two peaces.
fact: «Peace treaties» are agreements that end wars.
fact: «Make peace» means to become friends again after a quarrel.
fact: «Keep the peace» means stop fights and keep things calm.
fact: «Pax Mongolica» (the Mongol peace) describes a time when the lands were peaceful enough for traders to travel safely across Asia.
exercise: «After the Battle of Kadesh, Egypt and the Hittites signed one of the oldest known peace treaties.» What does peace mean in this sentence? | Getting along with others without arguing | Feeling sleepy after a long day | Quiet and calm, with no noise | *A time with no war or fighting
exercise: What does «make peace» mean after a quarrel? | To build a wall | *To become friends again after a quarrel | To hide a secret | To shout at each other
exercise: «Her room was full of peace and quiet, so she could finally read.» What does peace mean here? | Speaking very loudly | A time with no war | Being lost in a big crowd | *Calm, with no noise or worry
test: Which sentence uses peace correctly? | There were two peaces in the park. | Peaces are very nice. | *There was peace in the park. | The peaces were loud.
test: What does «keep the peace» mean? | *Stop fights and keep things calm | Sing a song loudly | Hide the peace in a box | Keep a secret from everyone
exam: «Traders could travel safely across Asia during the Mongol peace.» What does peace mean? | A loud party with music | Sleeping in a tent | Something good to eat | *A time with no war or fighting
